<ac:structured-macro ac:name="details"><ac:parameter ac:name="id">dbsec-platform</ac:parameter><ac:rich-text-body><table><tbody><tr><th><p>Platform</p></th><td><p>MySQL</p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Product</p></th><td><p>MySQL Community / Enterprise Server (InnoDB Cluster, replication)</p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Versions in scope</p></th><td><p><em>[e.g., 8.0, 8.4 LTS]</em></p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Policy</p></th><td><p><code>SEC-POL-DB-001</code></p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Technical basis</p></th><td><p>CIS Oracle MySQL Community / Enterprise Server 8.0 Benchmark</p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Tenable audit file(s)</p></th><td><p>CIS_MySQL_8.0_*.audit (database checks) + Unix audit for my.cnf and file permission checks</p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Tenable credential</p></th><td><p>Database credential, type MySQL (TCP port; one entry per instance)</p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Control prefix</p></th><td><p><code>MYSQL</code></p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Instances in scope</p></th><td><p><em>[count or link to CMDB]</em></p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Controls</p></th><td><p>12</p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Automated (Tenable)</p></th><td><p>7 of 12</p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Compliance % (last scan)</p></th><td><p>0%</p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Open CRITICAL / HIGH</p></th><td><p>0</p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Last Tenable scan</p></th><td><p>YYYY-MM-DD</p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Owner team</p></th><td><p><em>[Team]</em></p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Next review due</p></th><td><p>YYYY-MM-DD</p></td></tr></tbody></table></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
<ac:structured-macro ac:name="warning"><ac:parameter ac:name="title">Company policy – SEC-POL-DB-001</ac:parameter><ac:rich-text-body><p>This page is part of the company Database Security Configuration Policy (SEC-POL-DB-001). Its requirements are mandatory for every database in scope. Deviations need an approved entry in the DB Security – Exceptions Register. CIS Benchmarks and Tenable audit files are the technical basis and assessment method; where this policy differs from CIS, this policy applies.</p></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
<ac:structured-macro ac:name="toc"><ac:parameter ac:name="maxLevel">2</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro>
<h2>Scope &amp; applicability</h2>
<ul><li>MariaDB and Percona Server are in scope with this page as the baseline; differences are noted in Comments.</li><li>Configuration-file controls (<code>my.cnf</code>) are checked through the Unix (SSH) part of the scan.</li><li>Managed services (Amazon RDS / Aurora, Azure Database for MySQL): host and file controls are N/A.</li></ul>
<h2>Tenable assessment setup</h2>
<table><tbody><tr><th><p>Item</p></th><th><p>Value</p></th></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Scan template</strong></p></td><td><p>Policy Compliance Auditing (credentialed)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Audit file(s)</strong></p></td><td><p>CIS_MySQL_8.0_*.audit (database checks) + Unix audit for my.cnf and file permission checks</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Credential</strong></p></td><td><p>Database credential, type MySQL (TCP port; one entry per instance)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Scan account privileges</strong></p></td><td><p><code>SELECT</code> on <code>mysql.*</code> and <code>performance_schema.*</code>, <code>PROCESS</code>; no SUPER or administrative grants</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Tailoring</strong></p></td><td><p>Company values from the register below override CIS defaults in the tailored audit file. Store it in <em>[repository / Tenable policy name]</em></p></td></tr></tbody></table>
<h2>Control register</h2>
<ac:structured-macro ac:name="info"><ac:parameter ac:name="title">How to maintain this register</ac:parameter><ac:rich-text-body><ul><li>One row per control. Control IDs are never renumbered or reused.</li><li><strong>Tenable Check</strong> describes what the audit item reads and its pass condition. Copy the CIS section from the audit item's <code>reference</code> field into <strong>CIS Reference</strong>.</li><li>Changing a Compliant Value is a policy change: record it in the change log and get approval.</li><li>After every scan, update Compliance % and Open CRITICAL / HIGH in the table at the top of the page.</li></ul></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
<table><tbody><tr><th><p>Control ID</p></th><th><p>Control Name</p></th><th><p>Domain</p></th><th><p>Requirement</p></th><th><p>Severity</p></th><th><p>Compliant Value</p></th><th><p>Tenable Check (Audit / Query)</p></th><th><p>CIS Reference</p></th><th><p>Assessment</p></th><th><p>Last Review (Date / By)</p></th><th><p>Comments</p></th></tr><tr><td><p><strong>MYSQL-VER-001</strong></p></td><td><p>Supported release with security patches</p></td><td><p><code>VER</code></p></td><td><p>The server runs a supported release (8.0 until its EOL, or 8.4 LTS) at the latest patch level within the patch SLA.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Red</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">CRITICAL</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><code>SELECT VERSION()</code> in the approved version list</p></td><td><p><code>SELECT VERSION()</code></p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">PARTIAL</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>MYSQL-AAA-001</strong></p></td><td><p>No anonymous or wildcard admin accounts</p></td><td><p><code>AAA</code></p></td><td><p>No anonymous accounts exist; root and admin accounts cannot log in from any host.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Red</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">CRITICAL</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p>No row with <code>user = ''</code>; root only on <code>localhost</code>; no admin with <code>host = '%'</code></p></td><td><p>Query <code>mysql.user</code></p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Green</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">AUTOMATED</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>MYSQL-AAA-002</strong></p></td><td><p>Password validation component</p></td><td><p><code>AAA</code></p></td><td><p>Password strength validation enforces the corporate password standard.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">HIGH</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><code>validate_password.length</code> ≥ 14, <code>validate_password.policy</code> = MEDIUM or STRONG, <code>password_history</code> ≥ 10, <code>default_password_lifetime</code> ≤ 90</p></td><td><p><code>SHOW GLOBAL VARIABLES LIKE 'validate_password%'</code></p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Green</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">AUTOMATED</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p>Service accounts may use PASSWORD EXPIRE NEVER when the password is rotated by PAM.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>MYSQL-AAA-003</strong></p></td><td><p>Failed-login lockout</p></td><td><p><code>AAA</code></p></td><td><p>Accounts lock after repeated failed logins (8.0.19+), or connection-control throttling is enabled.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Blue</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">MEDIUM</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><code>FAILED_LOGIN_ATTEMPTS</code> ≤ 5 and <code>PASSWORD_LOCK_TIME</code> ≥ 1 on human accounts</p></td><td><p>Query <code>mysql.user.User_attributes</code></p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">PARTIAL</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>MYSQL-PRIV-001</strong></p></td><td><p>Administrative privileges restricted</p></td><td><p><code>PRIV</code></p></td><td><p>FILE, SUPER, PROCESS, SHUTDOWN, CREATE USER, GRANT OPTION and dynamic admin privileges are held only by approved admin accounts.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">HIGH</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p>Grantees match the approved admin list</p></td><td><p>Query <code>mysql.user</code> and <code>mysql.global_grants</code></p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">PARTIAL</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p>Tenable lists grantees; the reviewer compares with the approved list.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>MYSQL-SVC-001</strong></p></td><td><p>Local file loading disabled</p></td><td><p><code>SVC</code></p></td><td><p>Clients cannot load local files into the server, and server-side file import / export is limited to one directory.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">HIGH</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><code>local_infile = 0</code>; <code>secure_file_priv</code> set to a dedicated directory or NULL</p></td><td><p><code>SHOW GLOBAL VARIABLES</code></p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Green</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">AUTOMATED</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>MYSQL-SVC-002</strong></p></td><td><p>Test database and sample data removed</p></td><td><p><code>SVC</code></p></td><td><p>The test database and any sample schemas are removed.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Grey</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">LOW</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><code>SHOW DATABASES</code> has no <code>test</code> database</p></td><td><p><code>SHOW DATABASES</code></p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Green</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">AUTOMATED</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>MYSQL-SVC-003</strong></p></td><td><p>Strict SQL mode</p></td><td><p><code>SVC</code></p></td><td><p>The server rejects invalid data instead of silently truncating it.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Grey</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">LOW</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><code>sql_mode</code> includes <code>STRICT_ALL_TABLES</code> or <code>STRICT_TRANS_TABLES</code></p></td><td><p><code>SELECT @@GLOBAL.sql_mode</code></p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Green</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">AUTOMATED</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>MYSQL-CRYPTO-001</strong></p></td><td><p>Secure transport required</p></td><td><p><code>CRYPTO</code></p></td><td><p>All client and replication connections use TLS 1.2 or higher.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">HIGH</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><code>require_secure_transport = ON</code>; <code>tls_version = TLSv1.2,TLSv1.3</code></p></td><td><p><code>SHOW GLOBAL VARIABLES LIKE '%tls%'</code></p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Green</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">AUTOMATED</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>MYSQL-LOG-001</strong></p></td><td><p>Error and audit logging</p></td><td><p><code>LOG</code></p></td><td><p>The error log is written to a protected location and an audit log plugin / component records connections and privilege changes.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">HIGH</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><code>log_error</code> set; audit log plugin active (Enterprise Audit, Percona or MariaDB audit plugin)</p></td><td><p><code>SHOW PLUGINS</code> / <code>SHOW GLOBAL VARIABLES LIKE 'log_error%'</code></p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">PARTIAL</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p>Community Edition has no bundled audit plugin; record the approved alternative.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>MYSQL-OS-001</strong></p></td><td><p>Dedicated service account and file permissions</p></td><td><p><code>OS</code></p></td><td><p>mysqld runs as a dedicated non-root account; data directory and config files are readable only by that account.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Blue</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">MEDIUM</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><code>mysqld</code> runs as <code>mysql</code>; <code>datadir</code> mode 750 or stricter; <code>my.cnf</code> not world-writable</p></td><td><p>Unix audit: process owner and file permission checks</p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Green</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">AUTOMATED</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>MYSQL-OS-002</strong></p></td><td><p>No clear-text passwords on disk or in environment</p></td><td><p><code>OS</code></p></td><td><p>Passwords are not stored in my.cnf, scripts, shell history or the MYSQL_PWD variable. Use the login path or a vault.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">HIGH</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p>No <code>password=</code> in option files; <code>MYSQL_PWD</code> unset</p></td><td><p>Unix audit: content check on option files</p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">PARTIAL</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p><em>[MYSQL-DOMAIN-NNN]</em></p></td><td><p><em>[Short control name]</em></p></td><td><p><em>[Domain]</em></p></td><td><p><em>[What must be true]</em></p></td><td><p><em>[CRITICAL / HIGH / MEDIUM / LOW]</em></p></td><td><p><em>[Value that passes]</em></p></td><td><p><em>[Audit item / query + pass condition]</em></p></td><td><p><em>[CIS §]</em></p></td><td><p><em>[AUTOMATED / PARTIAL / MANUAL / PLANNED / NOT FEASIBLE]</em></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p><em>[Caveats, exception IDs]</em></p></td></tr></tbody></table>
